    {
      "occurrenceId": "15d0c1fe0f9ea48867960451ebd511fd83b16c620a50ab5968200ead18ddfb00",
      "source": "docs/planning/ATTENTION_RETRIEVAL_WITNESS_SEARCH_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "6c454d50f82544b0d80ccd9bad1c318cca82d8d4320bcca414db7ccc8ad314ef",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/scope"
      },
      "text": "Exact EAM graph/rank with hypothetical positive encoded history and hypothetical presentation reinforcement. Actual source, selected capability, IDN and writers not executed.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "d56f0e138bdf08e8687fdb90793ce5c658eb4eb4589d9846da3a47c1b4a5b888",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/status"
      },
      "text": "EXECUTED — robustness probe of constraint C6 across fixture difficulty",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "3b449a35677e8e7e3f78f6713bb5bbe2b2f827b83d271d8f993d881f1d369a8e",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/motivation"
      },
      "text": "VER-C3-CONCERN-002 evaluated C6 against a single fixture whose crossover was 5/3. This tests whether that constraint is a property of the law or of the fixture.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "1cd215b5e7f26d1f930a28dd864a2a91110cd4ffc9988b0b7cfb91afb32744ef",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/declaredDomain/baseGap"
      },
      "text": "1/4 (x-recent at now−1 → base 1/2; y-associated at now−3 → base 1/4)",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "97d919a92fb56177bf59f17742d8409c8d428656fd0fdf593e225619c6fb8fef",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/declaredDomain/crossoverFormula"
      },
      "text": "omega* = (base_x − base_y) / (pull_y − pull_x)",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "81f646752589f43fe6c34272723fa8a09e2536bcf19955d5a2a45c079731b9c5",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/structuralCeiling/statement"
      },
      "text": "R(q) = f(g·q) is bounded above by 1 for every gain, so omega_A = 1 + R is bounded above by 2 across the entire candidate family. A attains 2 exactly at q=1; every C attains it only in the limit of infinite gain. No member can exceed it.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "9c306919cfe416b24192966f7812646305cd150594a49b8b81c174c942119b73",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/0"
      },
      "text": "C6 is fixture-relative, as suspected. Every law reorders an easy fixture (crossover 6/5); no law reorders a hard one (crossover 2/1 or above). The constraint is only discriminating in the band between.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "abc52495acd0f5a9155b377605c27f39a4cfecff5ba168835d06d924497762a5",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/1"
      },
      "text": "The family has a hard structural ceiling of omega_A = 2, because R = f(g·q) is bounded by 1 for every gain. Raising the gain to 10 or 100 does not rescue a crossover at or above 2 — the limit is the bounded response itself, not the calibration.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "988320d56365799071df85e5be65952df1bce13686403eb204d6820abe46ddf1",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/2"
      },
      "text": "Candidate A is the unique member that ATTAINS the ceiling, and it does so precisely by paying E(1) = 0. Within this family, maximum retrieval amplification and non-annihilating encoding are in direct tension at the boundary; the decoupling buys a strictly interior region, not an escape from the trade.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "7261bd1a36027d61264ae184a3a6c06b0c656c4066599c6b774fe6031b253ea5",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/3"
      },
      "text": "The original 5/3 fixture sits inside the discriminating band, so VER-C3-CONCERN-002 is not vacuous: B genuinely cannot reorder it and A and C genuinely can. The conclusion stands for fixtures in that band and only there.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "344fb3c7aea3868feb2eedc83f404d431bb48276504a49b465ea42913ebc73fc",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/findings/4"
      },
      "text": "The effect is not an artifact of top-1 selection: over four episodes at K=2 the selected SET changes with q, so concern reorders membership and not merely the winner.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "e77f3f10403fec92fdedfbddad33fa36bf0966f300df75610c5a5d5c9f960088",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/consequences/0"
      },
      "text": "C6 must be restated as fixture-relative before it can serve as an acceptance criterion. \"omega_A can pass THE crossover\" is not well-formed; \"omega_A can pass the crossover of a declared corpus fixture\" is.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "bfb3801f4858a5092c5f4d99d8b181f87dfa1a9396a44a9f5365f57a95d506ef",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/consequences/1"
      },
      "text": "If a required phenomenon ever needs reordering against a recency advantage whose crossover is at or above 2, no member of this family can supply it, and the bounded-response choice for R — not the gain — is what must be revisited.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "7af74271d24edad21cdc1a1ee5f12cb404d4f9d2451469f2905bc24c341da70a",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/consequences/2"
      },
      "text": "That is a question about the bound on R, which OD-C3-002 constraint C7 requires to be bounded but does not fix the value of. A family with R bounded by 2 (omega_A <= 3) is a different family and a legitimate future comparator.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "559396878c2faf4b8ecaba780d6f382e7b2809bc6b44afee060acf6bb1a7e675",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/0"
      },
      "text": "Pure arithmetic at component scope. No identity, canonical record, allocation, record type, public ingress, state writer or corpus promotion. No source modified.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "17a7dbaaa6679333a3983635abef0044ecd97f70150553c24eb3c1b3dbac16fa",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/1"
      },
      "text": "One base-gap value and one pull-x value; the crossover was varied only through pull-y. Varying lambda, the decay exponent or presentation counts would move the bases and is untested.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "1f93191989dfc7ef49b041f03310b5b957735678bc32b02427ed714e32fcf89c",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/2"
      },
      "text": "This probe changes no verdict. It bounds the scope of VER-C3-CONCERN-002 rather than contradicting it.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    },
    {
      "occurrenceId": "1f3202c94ae0bbbdd3628a84905cb0f6cace1b0473be9b346898449e570a3228",
      "source": "docs/planning/CONCERN_RETRIEVAL_CEILING_REV1.json",
      "sourceSha256": "647cc5b77a29c9f23ea9d5f6ddad1d3b42b02975061c2e0ef7ec876c77d584dd",
      "location": {
        "pointer": "/limits/3"
      },
      "text": "PHEN-ATTN-001 receives no PASS.",
      "category": "NARRATIVE"
    }
  ],
